 {r}←parms ∆ProvokeCrash en
⍝ Signals the error `en` and lets HandleError process it, as Plodder's general trap would.
⍝ The error is light-weight: a plain `⎕SIGNAL`, with nothing to clean up afterwards.
⍝ The error number and the line it is signalled on make up the storm guard's signature,
⍝ so the same `en` always yields the same signature, and different numbers different ones.
⍝ Returns the number of HTML reports in the error folder afterwards.
 :Trap en
     {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}en                                  ⍝ The dfn makes the error happen on this line, inside the :Trap
 :Else
     :Trap parms.signal                             ⍝ `Process` signals this when it is done
         ##.HandleError.Process parms
     :EndTrap
 :EndTrap
 r←≢##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles parms.errorFolder,'/*.html'
⍝Done
